This Aporia License Agreement ("Agreement" or "License") is a legally binding
contract between you ("Licensee", "you", or "your") and Aporia.cc ("Licensor",
"we", "us", or "our") regarding your use of the Aporia software project,
including all source code, object code, documentation, assets, trademarks, and
related intellectual property (collectively, the "Software" or "Aporia").

By accessing, downloading, installing, copying, modifying, distributing, or
otherwise using the Software, you acknowledge that you have read, understood,
and agree to be bound by the terms and conditions of this Agreement. If you do
not agree to these terms, you must immediately cease all use of the Software
and destroy all copies in your possession or control.

The Software is a proprietary Minecraft client modification designed for
educational and personal use only. This License grants you limited, revocable,
non-exclusive, non-transferable rights to use the Software strictly in
accordance with the terms set forth herein.

================================================================================
                           SECTION 1: DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

For purposes of this Agreement, the following terms shall have the meanings
set forth below:

1.1  "Software" means the Aporia Minecraft client, including but not limited
     to all source code files, object code, compiled binaries, libraries,
     modules, plugins, extensions, APIs, SDKs, documentation, user interfaces,
     graphics, sounds, music, videos, data files, configuration files, scripts,
     and any other materials provided by Licensor.

1.2  "Derivative Work" means any modification, adaptation, translation,
     revision, enhancement, improvement, derivative, or other work based upon
     or incorporating the Software, in whole or in part, whether created by
     you or by third parties acting on your behalf.

1.3  "Distribution" means any transfer, conveyance, sale, lease, license,
     sublicense, gift, assignment, or other disposition of the Software or
     any Derivative Work, whether for value or without consideration, including
     but not limited to electronic transmission, physical media distribution,
     or making available through network services.

1.4  "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is intended for or
     results in commercial advantage, monetary compensation, or financial gain,
     whether direct or indirect, including but not limited to sale of products
     or services, advertising revenue, subscription fees, or donation solicitation.

1.5  "Malicious Use" means any use of the Software that is intended to cause
     harm, damage, or unauthorized access to computer systems, networks, data,
     or services, including but not limited to hacking, cracking, phishing,
     malware distribution, denial of service attacks, or unauthorized data
     extraction.

1.6  "Cheat Software" means any software, modification, or enhancement designed
     to provide unfair advantage in multiplayer games, bypass game mechanics,
     circumvent anti-cheat systems, or violate the terms of service of any
     game or online service.

1.7  "Authorized Purpose" means personal, non-commercial use of the Software
     for educational purposes, research, or private experimentation, excluding
     any Malicious Use or Commercial Use.

1.8  "Intellectual Property Rights" means all patents, copyrights, trademarks,
     trade secrets, moral rights, database rights, design rights, and any
     other intellectual property rights, whether registered or unregistered,
     anywhere in the world.

