     fees, expert witness fees, and travel expenses.

67.3 **Documentation**: Costs and expenses shall be documented.

67.4 **Taxation**: Costs shall be taxed by the court if
     applicable.

67.5 **Security**: The court may require security for costs.

================================================================================
                   SECTION 68: PRE-JUDGMENT INTEREST
================================================================================

68.1 **Interest**: Pre-judgment interest shall accrue on any
     award at the maximum rate permitted by law.

68.2 **Calculation**: Interest shall be calculated from the
     date of breach to the date of judgment.

68.3 **Compounding**: Interest shall compound monthly.

68.4 **Post-Judgment**: Post-judgment interest shall accrue
     at the statutory rate.

68.5 **Priority**: Interest shall be paid before principal.

================================================================================
                    SECTION 69: SPECIFIC PERFORMANCE
================================================================================

69.1 **Equitable Relief**: Licensor shall be entitled to seek
     specific performance of this Agreement.

69.2 **Irreparable Harm**: You acknowledge that breach of this
     Agreement may cause irreparable harm.

69.3 **Inadequate Remedy**: You acknowledge that monetary
     damages may be inadequate.

69.4 **No Bond**: Licensor shall not be required to post bond
     for equitable relief.

69.5 **Cumulative**: Equitable remedies shall be cumulative
     with other remedies.

================================================================================
                    SECTION 70: INJUNCTIVE RELIEF
================================================================================

70.1 **Injunction**: Licensor shall be entitled to seek
     injunctive relief for breach of this Agreement.

70.2 **Temporary Restraining Order**: Licensor may seek
     temporary restraining orders without notice.

70.3 **Preliminary Injunction**: Licensor may seek preliminary
     injunctions upon showing of likelihood of success.

70.4 **Permanent Injunction**: Licensor may seek permanent
     injunctions upon showing of actual breach.

70.5 **Contempt**: Violation of injunctions may result in
     contempt proceedings.

================================================================================
                    SECTION 71: DAMAGES CALCULATION
================================================================================

71.1 **Actual Damages**: Actual damages shall be calculated
     based on proven losses.

71.2 **Lost Profits**: Lost profits may be recovered if
     proven with reasonable certainty.

71.3 **Consequential Damages**: Consequential damages are
     excluded as provided herein.

71.4 **Mitigation**: Damages shall be mitigated where
     possible.

71.5 **Certainty**: Damages must be proven with reasonable
     certainty.

================================================================================
                    SECTION 72: STATUTORY DAMAGES
================================================================================

72.1 **Availability**: Statutory damages shall be available
     where provided by law.

72.2 **Copyright**: Statutory damages for copyright infringement
     shall be available under applicable law.

72.3 **Willfulness**: Willful infringement may result in
     enhanced statutory damages.

72.4 **Innocence**: Innocent infringement may result in
     reduced statutory damages.

72.5 **Election**: Plaintiff may elect statutory damages
     instead of actual damages.

================================================================================
                     SECTION 73: ACTUAL DAMAGES
================================================================================

73.1 **Compensatory**: Actual damages shall compensate for
     proven losses.

73.2 **Direct**: Direct damages flow directly from the breach.

73.3 **Proof**: Actual damages must be proven with evidence.

73.4 **Foreseeability**: Damages must have been foreseeable
     at the time of contracting.

73.5 **Causation**: There must be causal connection between
     breach and damages.

================================================================================
                   SECTION 74: CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES
================================================================================

74.1 **Exclusion**: CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARE EXCLUDED AS
     PROVIDED IN SECTION 14.

74.2 **Definition**: Consequential damages include indirect,
     incidental, and special damages.

74.3 **Examples**: Examples include lost profits, lost data,
     and business interruption.

74.4 **Exception**: Consequential damages may be recoverable
     for willful misconduct.

74.5 **Waiver**: You waive any right to consequential damages
     to the extent permitted by law.

================================================================================
                    SECTION 75: PUNITIVE DAMAGES
================================================================================

75.1 **Availability**: Punitive damages may be available for
     willful, malicious, or fraudulent conduct.

75.2 **Standard**: Punitive damages require clear and convincing
     evidence of wrongful conduct.

75.3 **Ratio**: Punitive damages shall bear reasonable ratio
     to actual damages.

75.4 **Caps**: Punitive damages shall be subject to statutory
     caps where applicable.

75.5 **Insurance**: Punitive damages may not be insurable.

================================================================================
                    SECTION 76: LIQUIDATED DAMAGES
================================================================================

76.1 **Agreement**: Parties agree that certain damages may be
     difficult to calculate.

76.2 **Reasonable Estimate**: Liquidated damages shall be a
     reasonable estimate of actual damages.

76.3 **Not Penalty**: Liquidated damages shall not be a penalty.

76.4 **Exclusive**: Liquidated damages may be the exclusive
     remedy for certain breaches.

76.5 **Cumulative**: Liquidated damages may be cumulative
     with other remedies.

================================================================================
                       SECTION 77: RESTITUTION
================================================================================

77.1 **Availability**: Restitution may be available to prevent
     unjust enrichment.

77.2 **Measure**: Restitution shall be measured by benefit
     conferred.

77.3 **Return**: Restitution may require return of property
     or benefits.

77.4 **Offset**: Restitution may be offset by damages.

77.5 **Equitable**: Restitution is an equitable remedy.

================================================================================
                      SECTION 78: DISGORGEMENT
================================================================================

78.1 **Availability**: Disgorgement may be available for
     willful breaches.

78.2 **Measure**: Disgorgement shall be measured by profits
     gained.

78.3 **Calculation**: Profits shall be calculated net of
     expenses.

78.4 **Burden**: The burden of proving expenses shall be on
     the breaching party.

78.5 **Cumulative**: Disgorgement may be cumulative with
     other remedies.

